  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Narsimha Siddigari vs The State Of Telangana on 23 July, 2025 Author: N.Tukaramji Bench: N.Tukaramji The Honourable Sri Justice N.Tukaramji Criminal Petition No. 9148 Of 2025 Order",
    "facts": "2. The petitioners are arrayed as accused Nos.1 and 2 in C.C.No.162 of 2025 registered for the offences punishable under Sections 317(2) of Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhitha, 2023 and Section 106(1) of BNSS and Section 3, 146, 130 r/w 177 of MV Act. 4. The prosecution case in brief is that the petitioners/accused Nos.1 and 2 are involved in selling and purchasing the banned Tobacco products and the Police concerned has seized the said Tobacco products worth of Rs.2,00,000/- from the possession of the petitioners. As per the prosecution, on 11.12.2024 at 16.00 hours, the complainant/Sub-Inspector of Police lodged a complaint alleging that the petitioners are illegally selling Pan Masala articles at Kalwakurthy, and retailing tobacco products by procuring from unknown persons and seized tobacco products 1) Vimal Pan Masala 208 x 4 = 832 packet (Each one packet 30 pouch), 2) VI Tobacco 4 bags each one bag 208 x 8 = 832 (Each one packet 30 pouch), 3)Jambo Meeraz two cottons each one cotton 35 packets, 4)RR Miraj 12 bags each one bag 42 3 NTR,J packet, 5) Swagath Tobaco 60 packet, 6) RR24 Pan Masala one cotton 50 box and 7)Navorathan Pan Masala 16 Boxes, total worth of Rs.2,00,000/- from the possession of the petitioners under the cover of panchanama.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioners would submit that a Coordinate Bench of this Court vide Criminal Petition Nos.3731 and Batch on considering similar allegations and the merits [LEAKAGE_MASK] the proceedings against the petitioner therein. He further submits that the 2nd respondent has registered the present crime in violation of the orders passed by this Court. Hence, prayed for quashment of the proceedings against the petitioners in the calendar case. 6. Learned Additional Public Prosecutor would submit that the petitioners have been found with the Tobacco products and investigation is pending. However fairly admitted that in the authority cited by the petitioners in the similar circumstances, the proceedings against the petitioners therein were [LEAKAGE_MASK]. 10. Having regard to similar factual position in the criminal petition relied on by the petitioner vide Crl.P.No.6235 of 2022 held that against the allegations of illegal sale and transportation of tobacco products the accusations under Sections 188, 269, 270, 272, 273, 278, 328 read 4 NTR,J with Sections 511, 336, 409 and 420 of I.P.C., cannot be maintained and [LEAKAGE_MASK] the proceedings against the petitioners therein.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioners would submit that a Coordinate Bench of this Court vide Criminal Petition Nos.3731 and Batch on considering similar allegations and the merits [LEAKAGE_MASK] the proceedings against the petitioner therein. 10. Having regard to similar factual position in the criminal petition relied on by the petitioner vide Crl.P.No.6235 of 2022 held that against the allegations of illegal sale and transportation of tobacco products the accusations under Sections 188, 269, 270, 272, 273, 278, 328 read 4 NTR,J with Sections 511, 336, 409 and 420 of I.P.C., cannot be maintained and [LEAKAGE_MASK] the proceedings against the petitioners therein.",
    "respondent_arguments": "He further submits that the 2nd respondent has registered the present crime in violation of the orders passed by this Court. Hence, prayed for quashment of the proceedings against the petitioners in the calendar case. 6. Learned Additional Public Prosecutor would submit that the petitioners have been found with the Tobacco products and investigation is pending. However fairly admitted that in the authority cited by the petitioners in the similar circumstances, the proceedings against the petitioners therein were [LEAKAGE_MASK].",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
